From: NanoKVM Enhanced maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sched: keep fair-class HRTICK disabled for NanoKVM

RC4 Linux 5.10 defaults HRTICK off. On Enhanced Linux 7.2.3 the
HRTIMER_REARM_DEFERRED branch enables it, adding scheduler timer interrupts
on the single 850 MHz C906. Live on/off repeats reduce Direct system CPU
at similar delivered traffic. Keep the deadline feature and high-resolution
timers unchanged. See firmware/cpu/HRTICK-VIDEO-2026-09-07.md for measurements
and qualification limits.

This is a NanoKVM board-tree policy, not a proposed global upstream default.

--- a/kernel/sched/features.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/features.h
@@ -66,7 +66,8 @@
 SCHED_FEAT(WAKEUP_PREEMPTION, true)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_HRTIMER_REARM_DEFERRED
-SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK, true)
+/* NanoKVM: avoid fair-class hrtick overhead on the single C906 CPU. */
+SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK, false)
 SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK_DL, true)
 #else
 SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK, false)
